# ADR-036 tombstone citation scope — CONSUMER POLICY (this repo owns it).
#
# `verdict retracted` and `done --cancel` refuse while a file matched here
# still cites the id being killed. Without this file the CLI falls back to
# the built-in default `docs/specs/**`, which matches ZERO tracked files in
# this repo — so from v0.9.22 until 2026-08-01 the gate reported "clean" on
# every id, including ids cited in the operations guide. An armed-looking
# gate that checks nothing is worse than no gate: it manufactures
# confidence. Committed 2026-08-01 after a coverage audit reproduced that.
#
# Lines are CLI globs filtered by match_paths (`*` stops at `/`, `**`
# spans) — never git pathspecs; a line starting ':', '-' or '!' is refused
# (SI-1), so exclusions cannot be expressed and the live corpus is
# enumerated positively instead.
#
# SCOPE = the live prose corpus. scripts/fact-health.sh EXPANDS THIS FILE
# for its inclusion list (since 2026-08-23, wk-1d000ad4), so the lockstep
# is now structural: edit this file and the sweep follows, because it has
# no list of its own to forget.
# Both answer one question — "which prose is a reader meant to act on today?"
# — so they must not drift apart. Until the refactor that sentence was a
# claim about consistency that nothing checked, and it was false by ten
# files; the exclusions below stay in fact-health.sh, because SI-1 forbids
# spelling them here. Excluded here for the same reason they are
# excluded there: docs/archive/ (frozen verbatim), docs/reviews/ (a dated
# review record), docs/roadmap-v3.md (a history log) and docs/field-notes*
# (dated session records) correctly name ids that were live THEN, and must
# never block a retraction NOW. docs/growth-gate/ IS in scope: it declares
# "Status: PILOT LIVE" and its shelved designs are instructions awaiting a
# trigger, not records of the past.
#
# The ledger itself is excluded structurally by the CLI, not here — a
# retraction basis legitimately cites its predecessor.
README.md
AGENTS.md
docs/beads-integration-guide.md
docs/candidate-adoption-analysis-prompt.md
docs/independent-review.md
docs/truth-ledger-explained.md
docs/truth-ledger-loophole-map.md
docs/truth-ledger-operations-guide.md
docs/truth-ledger-paper-v3.md
docs/truth-ledger-tutorial.md
docs/diagrams/*.md
docs/growth-gate/*.md

